    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n432" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcĕo</span></b> , ui, 2, v. n.
		v. 2. acer, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>to be sour.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (of wine): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum, quod neque aceat neque muceat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato R.
					R. 148</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Fig.,
				<i>to be disagreeable</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mentio pectori acet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7, 6</span></i>
			
			<i>a med.</i></div>
